[h2]Fixed: the mod's own souls had no Epic or Legendary names[/h2]

[b]A player-visible naming bug, and the structural cause behind it.[/b] Soulvizier's souls come in three tiers, and the higher two are meant to read [i]Epic Soul of the Gaoler[/i] and [i]Legendary Soul of the Gaoler[/i]. Every soul inherited from Soulvizier did exactly that. Every soul this port added did not: all three tiers showed the same plain name, so there was no way to tell an Epic soul from a Legendary one by reading it.

[list]
[*][b]98 souls now show their tier.[/b] The Soul of the Gaoler, Charon, Dagon, the Broodmother, the Blood Cult High Priest and every other soul authored for this port now render the Epic and Legendary prefix the rest of the roster has always had.
[*][b]Nothing was renamed.[/b] The tier word sits in front of the existing name, so the normal tier reads exactly as it did before and the original Soulvizier souls were not touched at all.
[*][b]The cause was structural, not a typo.[/b] A soul's three tiers share one name and differentiate through a separate quality field. Every generator this port uses writes one set of values to all three tiers, and none of them ever set that field, so the defect would have repeated on the next soul added.
[*][b]A permanent gate so it cannot come back.[/b] The build now fails loudly if any soul's tiers would render the same name, or if a tier carries the wrong quality word. It is checked against the whole roster on every build, with no exception list.
[/list]

[i]This update changes item names only. No drop rate, loot table, stat, skill or map was touched. The Boar Snatcher orb fix, the Spartan Crypt entrance fix and the chest breadth work from the previous updates are all included.[/i]

[i]Credits: [b]amgoz1[/b] for Soulvizier and the emblem, used with permission - [b]soa[/b] for Soulvizier AERA, the merge base for this Anniversary Edition port - [b]Dragonlord[/b] for DRX.[/i]
